							],
							"documentation": "UC2 Log In: one sequence diagram with account lookup, optional password verification and one authentication alternative.\nMemberView reads credentials and calls MemberManager.LogIn. The illustrated lookup path assumes FindMemberByAccount returns a Member or null normally. CheckPassword is called only when member != null. passwordVerified is evaluated only after this check. Lookup errors return an error result and stop authentication before the subsequent Member calls and authentication guards, as described below the diagram.\nSuccess: retrieve memberId and role, create LoginSession, store it in the current user server session and return the existing LoginResult. Open the role home. Customer login automatically starts UC3 at its history retrieval step. Employee login has no history popup.\nAlternative 2a: missing account or mismatched password returns a failure result. Do not create a session or open home/history. Display the result and allow corrected credentials and a new user submission, or cancellation. Account lookup errors remain distinct from an absent account and permit no Member calls.\nAlternative 4a: employee login opens the employee home and skips customer history.\nAlternative 4b: UC3 distinguishes no history from lookup failure. Retry resumes UC3 retrieval and popup closure preserves successful authentication.\nEnglish diagram labels, natural-language guards and local return names introduce no new fields, operations, result properties or enums. Failure policies are summarized below the diagram. No initial-request guard or loop is used.",
